1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:06,460
Stop staring at me like that.

2
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:09,050
Wataru.

3
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:10,210
Look at me.

4
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:20,040
When we were apart, I was thinking
about you the whole time too.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,660
But sometimes I wonder
if you didn't miss me as much.

6
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:29,070
I felt the exact same way.

7
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,750
So I'm really happy.

8
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:37,240
If you were even a little bit jealous,
that would make me so happy.

9
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:43,320
I get it, I get it.
Now let me go.

10
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,360
Hold on a second.

11
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,280
I've been holding back a lot.

12
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:50,250
I know that too.

13
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,840
When summer break comes,
let's go on another pilgrimage.

14
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,380
This time, we'll go wherever you want.

15
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,980
Where I want to go, huh?

16
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,800
All the places I want to go are overseas.

17
00:01:05,390 --> 00:01:07,650
Then we'll have to work
hard at our part-time jobs.

18
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:08,770
Right?

19
00:01:10,110 --> 00:01:11,980
But putting going abroad aside for now,

20
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,600
let's go somewhere together.

21
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:15,990
Yeah.

22
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:17,880
I'll think about it.

23
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:25,120
I really wish summer break
would hurry up and get here.

24
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:31,040
I really wish summer break
would hurry up and get here.

25
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,800
What?

26
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:40,270
Nothing. I just remembered you said the exact
same thing in your second year of high school.

27
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,740
Did I?

28
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,060
You have a great memory.

29
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:46,950
Of course I remember.

30
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,290
I remember everything about that summer.

31
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,060
I just feel like, whether it
was back then or right now,

32
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:04,510
I'm the only one whose heart is racing.

33
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,500
Summer break, huh?

34
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,500
(Incoming Call: Saeki)

35
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,680
Saeki?

36
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,550
Wataru, I forgot to
mention something earlier.

37
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,020
Oh?

38
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:27,580
I was hoping you could help me
thank the senior who gave us the tickets.

39
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,900
Ah, Niimi-san.

40
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:31,053
I'll tell him.

41
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:35,520
Also, is it really okay
for Niimi-san to miss it?

42
00:02:35,650 --> 00:02:37,400
It's a rare advance screening, after all.

43
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,820
Ah, about that.

44
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:43,580
Actually, he originally
asked me to go with him.

45
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:45,449
Wait, really?

46
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:48,460
Of course, I was planning
to go with you too.

47
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:55,730
But I just felt like I wanted to
see it with you for the first time.

48
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:01,000
After I turned him down,
he just gave me the tickets.

49
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Huh?

50
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,180
Hello?

51
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,100
Saeki, are you still there?

52
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,180
I'm here.

53
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:16,290
You suddenly went quiet, so I
thought we got disconnected.

54
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:18,990
No, sorry about that.

55
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:20,820
I'm just really happy.

56
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,280
I see.

57
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:29,380
Hey.

58
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:33,530
It's a bit early, but can
you get May 1st off?

59
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:34,840
Huh?

60
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:35,920
Why?

61
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:38,690
Because it's your birthday.

62
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,220
Oh, right.

63
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,720
Okay.

64
00:03:46,721 --> 00:03:47,820
I'll ask for the day off.

65
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,640
Thanks.

66
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:51,450
And,

67
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:55,850
Are you not going to call
me by my first name anymore?

68
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:00,900
Ah.

69
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,260
Good night, Wataru.

70
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,020
Good night.

71
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,510
Chiharu.

72
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,860
And I had finally calmed down too.

73
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,400
Damn it.

74
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,060
It's all the phone's fault.

75
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:39,750
I shouldn't have called him.

76
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:16,700
"My Summer Of You" (Episode 8)

77
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:25,650
Toda-kun.

78
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:29,209
That friend from last time
is your movie buddy, right?

79
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:30,730
Is he not coming to see a movie again?

80
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:34,729
He's only a freshman, so
he's probably busy with classes.

81
00:06:34,730 --> 00:06:35,730
I see.

82
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,850
Does he have a girlfriend?

83
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,100
A girlfriend?

84
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:40,826
It's not like I'm interested
in him or anything.

85
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:42,650
I'm just purely curious
about a handsome guy.

86
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,020
So? Does he?

87
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,240
He probably has someone he's dating.

88
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,969
Why are you getting all shy, Toda-kun?

89
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:52,970
Huh?

90
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:55,030
Just bring him along next time.

91
00:06:55,130 --> 00:06:56,130
Right, Saito-san?

92
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:58,189
You'll give them discount coupons, right?

93
00:06:58,190 --> 00:06:59,510
Give them? Of course I will.

94
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:01,566
He's a precious handsome guy, after all.

95
00:07:01,590 --> 00:07:03,960
No, I mean, because he's Toda-kun's friend.

96
00:07:07,670 --> 00:07:08,930
But I guess you're right.

97
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:12,110
If he has a girlfriend,
he'd probably go see movies with her.

98
00:07:13,990 --> 00:07:15,970
Who knows?

99
00:07:18,470 --> 00:07:21,270
I'm going to change the posters over there.

100
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:30,650
We are dating, right?

101
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:35,960
Between college and our part-time jobs, we
surprisingly don't have much time to see each other.

102
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:40,970
Even when we do meet up lately,
the mood just isn't there.

103
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:47,380
My birthday?

104
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:51,379
No, no, no.

105
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:53,180
So what exactly are you
getting so shy about?

106
00:08:08,216 --> 00:08:12,326
I was overthinking things
yesterday and barely slept.

107
00:08:12,709 --> 00:08:15,122
[Calendar Notification:
Deadline for Report Submission]

108
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:23,330
This is a lifesaver. I think I
can submit my report on time.

109
00:08:23,690 --> 00:08:25,670
You're the best, Sekiguchi senpai.

110
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:26,710
Thank you so much.

111
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,800
Right, right?

112
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:35,140
Even though we're at different colleges, you
can totally count on me for general ed classes.

113
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:38,210
Sorry for taking up your
time before your shift.

114
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:41,810
Can I treat you to some
ice cream as a thank you?

115
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:43,970
No need.

116
00:08:44,350 --> 00:08:46,110
Just consider it my
birthday present to you.

117
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,610
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

118
00:08:47,850 --> 00:08:50,010
Then I'll gladly accept.

119
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:52,820
So, what about Wataru?

120
00:08:53,510 --> 00:08:55,366
Do you have any plans
after you submit your report?

121
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:56,530
Ah.

122
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,200
I have some plans.

123
00:09:00,930 --> 00:09:05,930
Don't tell me you got yourself a lover?

124
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,349
Alright, deal's off!
Give me back the report.

125
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:20,110
No, no, it's not like that.

126
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:22,280
I told you, it's for my part-time job.

127
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:25,730
Really?

128
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:26,940
Really.

129
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:33,360
You're not having someone cook you a
delicious homemade meal to celebrate, are you?

130
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,440
You're not, right?

131
00:09:36,110 --> 00:09:37,110
Right?

132
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:39,609
- No.
- You're not, right?

133
00:09:39,610 --> 00:09:40,610
- No.
- Really?

134
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:41,959
- Really?
- I'm serious.

135
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:45,080
There won't be any scenes of someone
chopping away with a kitchen knife, right?

136
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:58,320
You're super skilled at this.

137
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:01,890
My parents are often away for work,
so I cook pretty often.

138
00:10:02,450 --> 00:10:03,560
Even so, it's just average.

139
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:04,810
Really?

140
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:06,560
And that does it.

141
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:09,149
By the way, what fillings do
you want in your rice balls?

142
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,729
Wow, salmon, I guess.

143
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:11,610
Okay.
Tuna mayo.

144
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,440
Okay.

145
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,150
Mentaiko.

146
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:16,450
Alright, let's go with those.

147
00:10:16,451 --> 00:10:17,699
Awesome.

148
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,169
Let's make some rice balls then.

149
00:10:19,170 --> 00:10:20,930
Okay, I'll help too.

150
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:24,580
Put the amount you want to eat on here.

151
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,660
Press a little indent in the middle.

152
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:29,016
And put the filling in, right?

153
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,040
Yeah, exactly.

154
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:32,489
I'll make a tuna mayo one.

155
00:10:32,490 --> 00:10:33,490
- Tuna mayo?
- Yeah.

156
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:34,990
Take this,

157
00:10:35,286 --> 00:10:36,785
- Take this.
- This is really hard.

158
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:39,189
Put it here, and cover it up a bit.

159
00:10:39,190 --> 00:10:40,190
I see.

160
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:45,059
- Wataru!
- Whoa, the salmon is spilling out.

161
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:48,569
Wataru, you're supposed
to shape it into a rice ball.

162
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:49,570
Okay, okay.

163
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:50,699
How are you shaping it so well?

164
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:51,806
Just a little bit like this.

165
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:53,090
Look, look.

166
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:56,390
How did it end up like this?

167
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:02,870
Oh, the thing I've been waiting for.

168
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:04,620
Are you sure you want to eat this?

169
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:09,120
Yeah, ever since I watched "The Chef of
South Polar," I've been dying to eat this.

170
00:11:09,290 --> 00:11:10,670
That's good then.

171
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:12,410
Well then.

172
00:11:13,090 --> 00:11:14,330
Let's eat.

173
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:17,630
I'll have the tuna mayo then.

174
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:21,400
Mmm, it's delicious!

175
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,720
Freshly made rice balls are the best.

176
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:27,689
The way you eat, Wataru,
makes it look really delicious.

177
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:29,270
Hmm? Does it?

178
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:32,609
By the way, why are you eating mine?

179
00:11:32,610 --> 00:11:34,900
I just wanted to eat
the rice ball you made.

180
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,230
You're so weird.

181
00:11:36,690 --> 00:11:38,630
Ah, I'll go get some drinks.

182
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:40,649
I'll help too.

183
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:41,650
Okay.

184
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:44,529
Do you want to drink some alcohol?

185
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,589
Huh? But you can't drink yet.

186
00:11:46,590 --> 00:11:47,830
That's true.

187
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:50,450
But you're already twenty,
so you're legally allowed to drink now.

188
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:55,010
We'll drink together
after your birthday passes.

189
00:11:57,170 --> 00:11:59,610
I'll save it for June 6th.

190
00:12:14,950 --> 00:12:17,920
I really do love that about you, Wataru.

191
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,250
Don't say it in such a serious tone.

192
00:12:24,190 --> 00:12:26,030
Can I kiss you?

193
00:12:29,950 --> 00:12:31,540
I guess so.

194
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:38,920
You startled me.

195
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:42,340
Ah, it's a message from Guchi.

196
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:43,930
Hmm?

197
00:12:43,931 --> 00:12:45,800
Happy 20th birthday again.

198
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:47,490
Stay lovey-dovey forever.

199
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:49,810
Love, Guchi. Heart.

200
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,080
Are you really at your part-time job?

201
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:54,440
What is it?

202
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:56,280
Just thinking about how close you guys are.

203
00:12:56,926 --> 00:12:58,556
Even though he beat me to it...

204
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,030
Wataru.

205
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:02,860
Happy birthday.

206
00:13:03,310 --> 00:13:04,589
Here's your present.

207
00:13:04,590 --> 00:13:06,570
Wow, thanks!

208
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:08,379
Oh, can I open it now?

209
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:09,380
Of course.

210
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:12,000
I wonder what it is.

211
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:17,960
Whoa, awesome!
It's "The Jet-Black Hawk"!

212
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:22,569
Hey, looking at this makes
me want to watch a movie.

213
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:23,900
I figured you'd say that.

214
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:25,650
Seriously?

215
00:13:38,710 --> 00:13:41,480
Hey, we can keep watching, right?

216
00:13:41,670 --> 00:13:45,780
Alright, let's pull an all-nighter
watching movies today.

217
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:49,910
Can't we?

218
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,580
No, it's fine.

219
00:13:53,590 --> 00:13:54,890
What should we watch next?

220
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,010
He fell asleep.

221
00:14:29,590 --> 00:14:30,590
Huh? Is it morning...?

222
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:32,230
Morning...?

223
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:55,810
Chiharu...?

224
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:00,900
Wataru, you're awake?

225
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,150
Good morning.

226
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:03,800
Good morning.

227
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:06,820
I tried to wake you up,
but you were out cold.

228
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:09,649
Ah, is it okay that you didn't go home?

229
00:15:09,650 --> 00:15:10,950
It's fine. Totally fine.

230
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:14,660
Actually, I'm the one who should apologize
for falling asleep while watching.

231
00:15:15,830 --> 00:15:17,729
And sorry for making
you sleep on the couch.

232
00:15:17,730 --> 00:15:19,370
No, it's totally fine.

233
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,129
I wanted to sleep next to you.

234
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:24,129
But you toss and turn too much.

235
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:25,130
Huh?

236
00:15:26,090 --> 00:15:27,330
Just kidding.

237
00:15:28,650 --> 00:15:29,929
It's too cramped for two people.

238
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:32,406
Plus, I was afraid I'd embarrass
you by hugging you in my sleep.

239
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:36,450
But I got to see your sleeping face a lot,
so I'm already satisfied.

240
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,440
How can he act so nonchalant about it?

241
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:51,149
Since it was my birthday,

242
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:54,160
I thought maybe something
like that would happen...

243
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,290
I had a great birthday.

244
00:16:04,990 --> 00:16:05,990
Thanks.

245
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,270
He's so sly.

246
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,990
Still unread.

247
00:16:33,690 --> 00:16:35,950
I'm exhausted.

248
00:16:36,070 --> 00:16:37,849
Today was brutal.

249
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:39,669
Golden Week is no joke.

250
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:41,750
"Blueprint" is super
popular right now, too.

251
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,249
The audience is really young.

252
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,930
Everyone's probably going on a
pilgrimage to the filming locations.

253
00:16:46,370 --> 00:16:48,920
Ah, Toda-kun, you went
with Saeki-kun before, right?

254
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:50,340
Huh?

255
00:16:50,341 --> 00:16:52,969
Ah, Saeki just invited me, that's all.

256
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:54,719
Wow, that's so nice.

257
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:58,100
In what universe do you get
invited by a handsome guy?

258
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,770
I see.

259
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,540
Hmm?

260
00:17:03,190 --> 00:17:05,730
Saeki-kun seems cool and aloof,

261
00:17:06,230 --> 00:17:08,510
but he's surprisingly proactive
about this kind of thing.

262
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:12,650
Huh...?

263
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:20,050
Does he feel the same way I do?

264
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:24,470
Can I kiss you?

265
00:17:35,070 --> 00:17:36,070
That's weird.

266
00:17:36,590 --> 00:17:38,350
Still unread.

267
00:18:03,790 --> 00:18:06,790
I heard he transferred schools.

268
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:37,360
Wataru, what's wrong?

269
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:40,030
Thank goodness...

270
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:47,000
You didn't read my
messages or answer my calls.

271
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:49,370
I figured something was wrong.

272
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,960
Sorry.

273
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:55,230
After you left,
I felt a bit weak and fell asleep.

274
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,650
But it's nothing serious.

275
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,960
38.4 degrees...

276
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,880
It's definitely because
you slept on the couch.

277
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,240
I'm really sorry.

278
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,820
It's not like that.

279
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,660
I already took some medicine.

280
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,340
I'm fine now.

281
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,890
- See?
- No, wait, hold on.

282
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:29,220
Why are you trying to kick me out?

283
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:32,080
No, it'd be bad if you caught it.

284
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:35,210
I never catch colds. It's fine.

285
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:37,719
But it's a rare long weekend...

286
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,840
Oh, stop nagging.

287
00:19:41,090 --> 00:19:42,090
Seriously.

288
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:45,060
If I were sick in bed with a fever,
how would you feel?

289
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,040
I'd want to take care of you.

290
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,410
Exactly.

291
00:19:58,190 --> 00:19:59,240
Alright.

292
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:02,070
Add this in.

293
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,990
There we go.

294
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,410
Okay, this should be right, yeah?

295
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:18,010
This should do it... right?

296
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,440
Is this really okay?

297
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:34,980
It's delicious.

298
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:36,700
Thank you.

299
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:39,500
Yeah, I'm glad.

300
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:46,200
Is there anything else you need help with?

301
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,540
Cleaning, laundry, whatever you need.

302
00:20:48,910 --> 00:20:51,470
Ah, if you're sleepy,
don't hold back, just go to sleep.

303
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:55,430
I'll just read a bit
while keeping an eye on you anyway.

304
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:58,310
You look like you're having fun.

305
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:01,510
No, it's not like I'm
gloating over your misery.

306
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,930
I know.

307
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:07,890
I just feel bad
making you take care of me.

308
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,160
You know,

309
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,076
even though you usually do
this kind of thing so naturally,

310
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:19,420
I'm not used to it at all,
so I always end up fumbling around.

311
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:24,860
That's why I've always
thought you were so sly.

312
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:28,980
But,

313
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:32,290
I can tell you're trying really hard.

314
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:40,560
So at times like this,
I want to step up and show what I can do.

315
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,526
I feel like my temperature
is going up again...

316
00:21:47,550 --> 00:21:48,550
Huh?

317
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,680
Then...

318
00:21:54,810 --> 00:21:56,650
Can I ask you for a favor?

319
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,750
I want you to hold my hand.

320
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:13,660
Okay.

321
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:33,370
What's wrong? Can't sleep?

322
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:34,720
No.

323
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,820
I just feel like it's a
waste to fall asleep.

324
00:22:37,540 --> 00:22:38,540
Plus,

325
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:43,380
it's frustrating that I want to kiss you
but I can't.

326
00:22:43,610 --> 00:22:44,610
Huh?

327
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:46,340
Sorry, sorry.

328
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:48,700
I'm bothering you again, aren't I?

329
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,930
Well... it's not like you can't.

330
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,210
If it's just a quick kiss.

331
00:23:01,290 --> 00:23:02,290
Eh...

332
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:05,760
No way.

333
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:07,780
I don't want to get you sick.

334
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:14,040
Then...

335
00:23:16,770 --> 00:23:18,520
Through the mask.

336
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:51,900
(Akiyoshi: Let's go to the next
study abroad info session together.)

337
00:24:45,860 --> 00:24:47,779
(Next Episode Preview) I'm planning
to build up a high tolerance for alcohol.

338
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:49,779
That's totally jinxing it, right?

339
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:51,660
You wanted to kiss me just now, right?

340
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:54,510
Am I going to hold him back?

341
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:56,300
Wataru.

342
00:24:56,580 --> 00:24:58,830
Actually, I wanted to tell you in person.
